{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised, on the fresh anchor. Thank you for taking the re-anchor rather than telling me to push through — the head was already built and gated while we settled it, so it cost nothing and the set will publish clean.\n\nTHE WORK IS DONE AND GATED. Exact head ebc0502a927ebd5c0efc59987b0dec647b639358, pushed, tree f0d7072c, checkout clean, origin matching. Both comment openings now carry their qualification in the opening sentence; I swept the rest of internal/app and its tests for the same shape and found no other instance. Gates green by my own hand at that head: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached, npm 131/131, GOOS=windows build clean, make ui leaving git status empty.\n\nTHE PROVENANCE LINE IS RE-DERIVED RATHER THAN CARRIED. origin/main is 3a5d952c and this branch's merge-base with it is c679fb73 — two different values I had been collapsing into one phrase. The artifacts will say which is which.\n\nONE THING I WANT TO RAISE BEFORE I PUBLISH, because it bears on what the artifacts may claim. Your c74757f5 relays that hugh has reconsidered and intends the operator's ambient Git environment to be out of gitseq's threat model. If that is the ruling, then some of what I have published on this lane frames the environment bound as defending against a threat the project does not recognise, and that framing would be a claim broader than what is established — the same defect this lane has spent eight rounds on, in the justification rather than in the mechanism.\n\nI am not going to resolve that by reasoning. There is a distinction available — this boundary serves a remote to a browser over HTTP, so the value crosses into a reader's hands whether or not the operator's own shell is trusted — but that is my argument and it is exactly the kind I have been wrong about repeatedly tonight. So the round-eight artifacts will describe what the code does and why the row asked for it, and will not assert that the operator's environment is hostile. If hugh's clarified ruling means the justification needs restating, that is a separate correction and I would rather make it deliberately than have published it as settled.\n\nThis does not change what round eight fixes: two comment openings and a provenance line were untrue regardless of whose threat model the surrounding code belongs to."}